  "2026-10-24T15:43:54.219Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 verification: pm test --run --only-last --progress ran node --test test/transfer-properties.test.ts test/ambient-defaults.test.ts test/transfer.test.ts test/transfer-cli.test.ts test/reconcile.test.ts test/reconcile-cli.test.ts test/import-paths.test.ts; 106/106 pass, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Includes actual SIGKILL recovery, 24 every-row interruption cases (three rows, four settings, chunk sizes 1 and 3), creation-to-ledger interruption, bootstrap and missing/corrupt ledger cases, edited/deleted pinned item replay, and two seeds 23404582/12648430 with 512 adversarial rows each (1024 total). Local transfer.ts V8 coverage is 100% lines/branches/functions. Typecheck, build, build:test, docstring lint (91 declarations across 12 sources) and whitespace checks pass; no separate lint script exists. Full unchanged npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26 remain required CI evidence after push. Existing project policy disables linked-test result persistence; this comment retains the counts."
  "2026-10-24T15:48:19.677Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 full release evidence on implementation head 4c9fc77d1c1ee898f2fb8b7dc8ec5c0a1bfc1a05: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40108341218 passes npm run release:check and bun run release:check on both Node 22 and Node 26. Every gate passes 464/464 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 12 declared sources, and docstring lint 91/91 declarations. Four gates total 1856 test executions; unchanged scope and thresholds. Fresh tracker health, audit, packing, changelog, release attestation and Bun dependency-graph installation pass. CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40108341231 passes. No new pm CLI/SDK defect found; pre-existing installer drift remains on pm-beads-v9r1. Claim is released, item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification, and no merge or release is performed. This evidence-only tracker commit will receive its own exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-24T16:38:39.559Z",codex-agent,"Round 3: pulled remote head 6806409; origin/main is already contained. Replacing in-band source identity with registered bead_id metadata across transfer, import, export and reconciliation. Preserve source descriptions verbatim; recognize only the historical exact terminal marker when structured identity is absent and report first-touch migration. Extend both seeded 512-row cases through transfer, export and upsert, with independent behavioral revert proofs."
  "2026-10-24T16:44:26.059Z",codex-agent,"Implementation now uses registered bead_id metadata for transfer/import/reconciliation and structured export/upsert matching. Legacy decoding is limited to the exact old terminal envelope, disabled whenever metadata is present; migration removes only that envelope and reports via stderr plus history. New full-pipeline tests exposed an existing argv transport gap for NUL descriptions; importer now sends descriptions through the host stdin contract to preserve arbitrary bytes. Focused transfer/identity tests passed; updating legacy-format expectations and validating the two 512-row seeds."
  "2026-10-24T16:50:29.515Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 behavioral revert proofs (each changed function reverted alone, then restored): (1) reverted transfer createOptions to marker-based descriptions; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"structured identity wins\" test/identity.test.ts failed 0/1 because bead_id was absent. (2) restored broad legacy scanning in legacyBeadIdentity; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"legacy fallback\" test/identity.test.ts failed 0/1 on an embedded marker. Separately disabling first-touch migration failed the same test 0/1. (3) reverted only pmItemToBead to ignore structured identity; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"seed 23404582\" test/transfer-properties.test.ts failed 0/1 after transferring/exporting 512 rows, proving the pipeline catches an incorrect exported id. All changes restored; identity tests passed 3/3 before additional opt-out/error coverage was added. No thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-24T16:50:35.273Z",codex-agent,"Transport correction: the host stdin contract normalizes CRLF, so NUL and literal-dash descriptions now use public SDK mutations with preserveMutationStdinTokenFields; normal argv mutations preserve their existing behavior. An empty bead_id is persisted for identity opt-out and id-less imports, preventing new user-authored suffixes from being mistaken for legacy identity. Reconciliation migration disables unrelated extensions and refreshes the returned metadata after mutation."
  "2026-10-24T17:00:07.788Z",codex-agent,"Focused verification: node --test test/identity.test.ts executed through pm test --run --only-last --progress passes 5/5, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Tests cover structured identity, exact legacy parsing and one-time reported migration, real import/export/upsert with NUL/CRLF/whitespace/literal dash, SDK validation/type fallback, and identity opt-out. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. Full unchanged coverage and npm/Bun release evidence remain in progress. Local health retains existing installer fence drift and extension host/package version skew; no history repair or unrelated configuration change is applied."
  "2026-10-24T17:03:01.005Z",codex-agent,"Broader restored-source verification: node --test --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=identity.ts --test-coverage-include=index.ts --test-coverage-include=reconcile.ts --test-coverage-include=transfer.ts test/identity.test.ts test/import-paths.test.ts test/export-diff-paths.test.ts test/helper-truth-tables.test.ts test/ambient-defaults.test.ts test/smoke.test.ts test/transfer.test.ts test/reconcile.test.ts passes 257/257, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Diagnostic coverage is 100% lines/branches/functions for identity.ts and reconciliation, and every newly introduced index.ts identity/transport branch is covered. This focused scope is not full-gate evidence; the unchanged full suite remains required on npm and Bun in CI. The seeded full pipeline retains two seeds with 512 rows each in a single receiving tracker per seed."
  "2026-10-24T17:05:09.272Z",codex-agent,"Legacy compatibility edge verified after implementation push: an incomplete marker prefix in the body is plain text that the old encoder could legitimately retain before appending its terminal envelope. Legacy recognition now rejects earlier complete markers using the historical bounded predicate, while retaining an incomplete prefix verbatim. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"legacy fallback\" test/identity.test.ts passes 1/1; typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass."
  "2026-10-24T17:07:59.782Z",codex-agent,"Full-pipeline orchestration correction: the expanded 512-item CLI upsert exceeds the existing full-suite timeout because each child rereads the whole receiver. Retain both 512-row seeds and the global 512-row serialization assertions, and execute every generated row through transfer/export/upsert/export in eight 64-row real non-git receivers per seed. Aggregate assertions require exactly 512 transfers and 512 intended updates per seed; no row, assertion, source scope, timeout or coverage threshold is removed or relaxed. The earlier single-receiver note describes the superseded harness. Full pipeline and CI validation continue on this bounded harness."
  "2026-10-24T17:17:47.593Z",codex-agent,"Final pipeline implementation supersedes the temporary batching harness: initialized local tracker creates, updates and relationship rewrites reuse the public SDK adapter with literal-description policy; the existing CLI transport remains for callers without an initialized local tracker. This avoids a new process and whole-tracker scan per mutation. Restore one 512-row receiving tracker for each seed, and derive every expected pm id from a certified complete list because receipt row details are intentionally bounded. Native targeted command (transfer-properties, identity, ambient-defaults, import-paths, reconcile-cli, smoke) passes 174/174. Both seeds complete transfer/export/upsert/export with exactly 512 intended updates each, correct source ids and byte-identical descriptions (1024 rows total). The linked identity test rerun passes 5/5 through pm test. Full isolated-HOME npm run coverage passes 471/471, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 13 source files, unchanged scope and thresholds, in about 158 seconds. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint (90 declarations/13 sources) and whitespace checks pass."
  "2026-10-24T17:28:09.745Z",codex-agent,"CI implementation run 40115489452: Node 22 passes its npm and Bun release gates; Node 26 passes all 471 tests but exposes two additional V8 branch counters in index.ts. Remove the unreachable empty-id fallback from matched upserts (a match necessarily has its normalized source id), and exercise the public converter with structured identity and an absent description. Node 26.12 local isolated-HOME npm run coverage now passes 471/471, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, with 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 13 sources. The five focused identity tests pass on Node 26 too. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. Verified the published peer-floor 2026.10.15 package exports the literal-field API; no dependency pin or peer range change is needed. Documentation distinguishes explicit SDK/export migration messages from the ordinary update history recorded by an upsert."
  "2026-10-24T17:34:41.378Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 full release evidence on implementation head 5305c726c0a99c5060c20b273a026d9b13527174: CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40116272866 passes npm run release:check and bun run release:check on both Node 22 and Node 26. Every gate passes 471/471 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, with 100% measured lines/branches/functions across all 13 declared sources and docstring lint 90/90 declarations. Four gates total 1884 test executions; source scope and thresholds are unchanged. Both 512-row seeds complete the full transfer/export/upsert/export pipeline in one receiving tracker per seed, with source ids, exact descriptions and intended upsert targets verified. Fresh tracker health, production audit, packing, changelog, release attestation and Bun graph installation pass. CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40116272854 also passes. Observed host stdin CRLF normalization and SDK type errors without CLI machine codes are handled by the tested SDK adapter; no upstream issue is filed. Existing local installer fence drift and extension host/package skew remain separate environment findings. The claim is being released, item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification, and no merge or release is performed. The evidence-only tracker commit will receive its own exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-24T17:49:13.021Z",codex-agent,"Round 4: remove all first-touch writes from export and reconciliation reads. Add one explicit identity migration command, dry-run by default, with per-item SDK beforeMutation hash guards; exercise concurrent edits and invocation author precedence. Verify read-only tracker bytes/history, behavioral revert proofs, targeted checks and npm/Bun CI release gates."
  "2026-10-24T17:52:41.243Z",codex-agent,"Implemented explicit beads migrate-identities preview/--apply and guarded migration in transfer apply. Reads now use the legacy suffix only in memory. Legacy upserts report a required explicit migration instead of migrating on touch. Added real non-git tracker tests for whole-tracker bytes/history, read-to-write interleavings, SDK lock serialization and three-level author precedence. npm ci reproduced the already tracked merge fence drift; restored only that generated fence change."
  "2026-10-24T17:58:45.792Z",codex-agent,"Guard interleavings pass at listed/read/before_schema/after_schema/before_update/locked boundaries using a separate SDK peer process at the lock boundary. Ordinary transfer apply must keep its existing foreign-record guarantee, so migration inside transfer apply requires the explicit --migrate-identities flag. Reconciliation replacing a legacy description requires explicit migration and a new plan to avoid losing fallback identity. Whole-tracker regression setup initializes SDK derived caches through core/SDK reads before the snapshot; no Beads command pre-runs. Pinned SDK cold reads write runtime caches, and core get writes a usage ledger; these are host limitations rather than migration writes and are being reported explicitly."
  "2026-10-24T18:03:18.437Z",codex-agent,"Additional checks cover annotation-only concurrent edits, deletion after listing and just before update, and invalid UTF-8 source refusal. The pinned SDK reports missing update targets with NOT_FOUND exit code but no machine code, so guarded migration recognizes that SDK outcome and reports the item as skipped. This SDK diagnostic gap is retained for the final report; no upstream issue is filed."
  "2026-10-24T18:06:21.986Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof 1: restored only the original export migration helper and first-touch call; npm run build succeeded and node --test --test-name-pattern=\"every read-only legacy command\" test/identity-migration.test.ts failed 1/1 at beads export with changed tracker bytes. Separately restored only the original reconciliation read migration function/call; rebuilt and the same test failed 1/1 at beads reconcile with changed history bytes on an acknowledged legacy tracker. Restored exact fixed implementation bytes and rebuilt after each proof. The test snapshots every file including runtime artifacts after fixture-only core/SDK cache initialization; it does not pre-run a Beads read."
  "2026-10-24T18:06:24.412Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof 2: removed only the beforeMutation whole-item hash comparison, kept the explicit command and author forwarding, rebuilt, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"migration previews by default and skips peer edits\" test/identity-migration.test.ts failed 1/1: the migrated old body replaced the peer description. Restored exact fixed bytes and rebuilt. The retained test covers listed, located, read, before_schema, after_schema, before_update and locked boundaries with genuine SDK peers; the locked peer runs in a separate process."
  "2026-10-24T18:06:26.198Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof 3: changed only the migration author resolver to ignore its invocation argument, rebuilt, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"explicit migration CLI history honors author\" test/identity-migration.test.ts failed 1/1: actual history author environment, expected reviewer. Restored exact implementation bytes and rebuilt. The CLI host can normalize --author into PM_AUTHOR, so the test checks both real CLI invocations and the direct SDK invocation boundary for explicit author, environment and package fallback."
  "2026-10-24T18:06:29.371Z",codex-agent,Cold-read all-files purity remains an explicit host limitation tracked by pm-beads-w90u. No runtime files are excluded from the initialized-cache byte comparison. This PR does not modify the SDK pin or upstream pm-cli. Existing missing native mutation preconditions remain upstream pm-cli#1576.
  "2026-10-24T18:09:13.695Z",codex-agent,"Restored linked regression run: npx pm --author codex-agent test pm-beads-tma4 --run --only-last --progress passes all 8 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. The read-purity test executes 15 real CLI read/planning/dry-run variants and SDK snapshot/plan reads against an acknowledged non-git legacy tracker, comparing every file byte including history and initialized runtime artifacts. The migration tests verify explicit and environment/package authors through both real CLI and direct SDK boundaries, guarded stale skips, queued peers under the item lock, annotations, vanished items, corrupt source reads, and reconciliation identity preservation."
  "2026-10-24T18:09:15.351Z",codex-agent,"Local typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint (13 sources, 91 documented declarations), and git diff --check pass. A separate local strict-health probe still reports the pre-existing merge fence drift and a global pm-github host-version skew; the installed package graph is unchanged. Full release gates run with an isolated HOME and git configuration, and CI fresh-clone health remains the gate for the pushed head."
  "2026-10-24T18:13:50.533Z",codex-agent,"The initial full isolated-HOME npm gate ran 479 tests: 475 passed and four old fixtures failed because they expected implicit migration during acknowledgement/upsert. Updated those fixtures to invoke explicit migration during setup. Coverage identified the old merge-strategy skip arm as bypassed by the new legacy check; moved that legacy-specific skip after the existing explicit skip policy. Focused fixture rerun passes 6/6, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, including compensation under ambient defaults and terminal/nonterminal upserts. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. CI npm plus Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds will provide the final full-suite evidence."
  "2026-10-24T18:20:23.755Z",codex-agent,"Code head 28fe0c1e8c76823c98d04ef5ecc5dbdec410161d is fully green in CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40119767864 . Verified the completed job logs: Node 22 npm 479/479 and Bun 479/479; Node 26 npm 479/479 and Bun 479/479. Every gate reports zero failures, skips, cancellations and todos, with 100% measured lines, branches and functions across all 13 intended source files at unchanged thresholds. Both fresh-clone strict tracker-health checks and Bun package-graph installations pass. Local linked migration and fixture regressions passed 8/8 and 6/6. All per-point behavioral revert receipts are retained above. This final metadata-only commit records the evidence and releases the claim; source code is unchanged and its CI will be checked before reporting the pushed head. No merge, release, upstream issue, mentions or thread replies were performed."
  "2026-10-24T18:24:38.280Z",codex-agent,"Final metadata-head CI run 40120263213 passed all 479 tests on Node 26, but correctly refused the npm release gate because an existing mutation-error branch was uncovered (99.97% lines, 99.95% branches). The old failed-update fixture still used a legacy identity, so it passed by taking the new migration-required skip rather than attempting the injected transport failure. Updated that fixture to an already structured identity and added a positive assertion that the failing update transport actually ran. Source implementation and all thresholds remain unchanged; this removes dependence on another test incidentally reaching that error path. The earlier full code-head CI evidence remains genuine, but it does not override this final-head coverage failure."
  "2026-10-24T18:25:48.753Z",codex-agent,"The deterministic transport regression now passes 1/1 through npx pm test pm-beads-tma4 --run --only-last --progress. It asserts an update with the intended title reached the transport before accepting the skipped-result/edge-resolution behavior. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. This commit changes only that fixture/assertion plus PM evidence; the identity/read/migration implementation remains byte-identical to code head 28fe0c1, whose earlier npm/Bun matrix passed 479/479 in each gate. Release the claim with this commit, and verify the new head in all four CI gates before the final report; the newer missing-coverage run is not counted as approval."
  "2026-10-24T23:18:20.389Z",codex-agent,"Round 5: auditing every tracker item lookup, file read, history read, type mapping and identity allocation. Replace package storage assumptions with pinned SDK operations; add real non-git tracker configuration matrix and behavioral revert proof. Remote PR head is current and already includes main."
  "2026-10-24T23:24:36.421Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 implementation: item-access.ts delegates identity generation to generateItemId with SDK-resolved configuration and registry, history to PmClient.run(history), and canonical documents to getItemAt. Transfer ownership and migration no longer locate files; reconciliation no longer resolves history paths or hashes source IDs into core IDs. Export, workspace diff and upsert use listAllComplete. Removed raw timestamp patching/history-repair; pinned SDK lacks source timestamp import/update. Found history command initializes missing streams, so a pure point-in-time read guards it. Testing 20 real non-git configuration/workflow matrix cases plus existing crash, peer-edit and history guards."
  "2026-10-24T23:28:39.967Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: restored only the previous ownership function and its SDK imports; all new tests and all other fixes stayed unchanged. Ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"SDK tracker matrix: custom type folders\" test/tracker-configurations.test.ts. Exit 1: 2 passed, 3 failed, 0 skipped. Apply, interrupt+resume and export fail with invalid_journal for Task configured in work. Restored the fixed ownership function immediately afterward. The original combined matrix and targeted run passed 79/79, and the pm-linked full matrix passed 20/20."
  "2026-10-24T23:30:26.090Z",codex-agent,"Restored proof result: the exact same custom-folder matrix command passes 5/5, 0 skipped. Added SDK item-access regressions for absent foreign history (no initialized stream), compacted durable versions and unrecorded item drift: 2/2 pass. Reconciliation reservation-ledger replay regression passes 1/1. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. npm release gate is running with isolated HOME and git identity. Local strict health separately reports existing global extension host-version skew and merge-fence drift tracked by pm-beads-v9r1; no history was repaired and the committed extension fence remains unchanged."
  "2026-10-24T23:47:16.644Z",codex-agent,"Full local npm release gate reached the unchanged 15-minute timeout; this is missing full-gate evidence, not a pass. One 512-row transfer/export/upsert seed passed before timeout. Review found and reproduced unpublished SDK ID reservation collisions using runWithReproducibleProcessEnvironment. Allocation now retries SDK-generated IDs against the batch reservation set, bounded at 32 attempts. Ownership uses SDK light metadata only for existence and SDK verification digests for new pins, with guarded legacy JSON-document-hash compatibility, avoiding repeated full-corpus body reads. Final targeted checks and final-head CI will verify these changes."
  "2026-10-25T00:00:05.983Z",codex-agent,"Final SDK boundary: readSettings and resolveItemTypeRegistry supply the complete context to SDK locateItem; readLocatedItem, getHistoryPath, readHistorySnapshot and verifyHistoryEntries perform every item/history resolution and read. No package item paths, folders, extensions or core ID formulas remain. SDK generateItemId supplies IDs with bounded unpublished-reservation collision retries. SDK verification digests pin current documents, retaining guarded compatibility with earlier JSON-document hashes. Export/diff/upsert use listAllComplete. Generic high-level canonical-ID reads fail after prefix drift, so the final adapter uses literal SDK store APIs. Non-filesystem state/reservation and literal-ID API gaps remain in pm-beads-z4k0."
  "2026-10-25T00:00:09.233Z",codex-agent,"Final local evidence: configuration matrix 20/20; settings and resume regressions 9/9; migration plus SDK item-access checks 11/11, no skips. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. Final behavioral ownership revert restored only the previous ownership function and SDK imports: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"SDK tracker matrix: custom type folders\" test/tracker-configurations.test.ts fails 3/5 with invalid_journal; restored fix passes 5/5. Reverting only the allocator collision guard fails node --test --test-name-pattern=\"SDK identity allocation retries\" test/item-access.test.ts (0/1); restored item-access tests pass 3/3. Final source bytes were restored. Initial full local npm gate timed out at the unchanged 15-minute limit; it is not passing evidence. Final full npm and Bun gates will run in CI on the pushed head: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/pull/165/checks . No coverage thresholds or timeouts changed."
  "2026-10-25T00:11:25.729Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40145086959 on 629aab4 executed 487 tests on Node 22 and 26: 483 passed and 4 failed in each npm gate, so Bun did not run. Failures exposed legacy SDK/CLI fallback behavior for unreadable roots and optional workspace validation, acknowledgement-file discovery after introducing reservation state, and a stdout test capturing Node binary test-runner IPC during new async SDK reads. Restored SDK metadata listing for optional dependency validation, retained the canonical CLI fallback when SDK tracker preflight fails, moved reconciliation reservations to their own transaction namespace, and moved the stdout assertion into an isolated real Node process. Node 22 also measured the impossible timestamp-success branch; removed that branch while retaining an explicit unsupported-API report and timestamped=0. Thresholds unchanged; targeted reproductions and final CI rerun pending."
  "2026-10-25T00:14:59.602Z",codex-agent,"CI correction verification passed 7/7 targeted cases: unsupported timestamps, missing timestamps, cross-workspace dependency fallback, identity schema-registration failure, RAW UTC deadline acknowledgement convergence, retained SDK reservation ledgers, and stdout suppression. The stdout check now verifies both the direct host-suppression API and exactly one JSONL record from a real isolated Node process; its focused rerun passes 1/1. Build, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. Reconciliation reservations are isolated under the package transaction namespace; optional workspace validation still uses the SDK metadata-list API. Final full npm/Bun evidence will come from the next exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-25T00:24:54.602Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40146002009 on 864d1ad passed every test in all four release attempts: 492/492 each, with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Node 26 npm/Bun and Node 22 npm also met all unchanged coverage thresholds. Node 22 Bun measured index.ts branch coverage at 99.88 percent (99.95 overall) and failed the gate. The workflow reports uncovered branches before Bun, so no branch coordinate was retained for that failure. Moved the existing failure-only diagnostic after both gates; release commands, matrices, thresholds and permissions remain unchanged. Final gate verification continues."
  "2026-10-25T00:32:25.912Z",codex-agent,"The relocated diagnostic identified the intermittent miss in CI run 40146614062: index.ts:2088, preserving an SDK preflight error other than NOT_FOUND before the legacy CLI fallback. Added SDK workspace export preserves a non-directory tracker error before CLI fallback, using a real temporary regular file and the real SDK. A Node 22 instrumented focused run passes 1/1 and records the previously missing branch with count 1. The complete SDK item-access linked test now covers four real-tracker cases; thresholds remain unchanged. This adds deterministic coverage of the error boundary rather than relying on incidental cases in another gate."
  "2026-10-25T00:36:00.187Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the previous instrumentation receipt: the first file-root-only run recorded DA:2088=1, a line hit, while BRDA:2088 remained zero. Expanded the same real-SDK regression to also call export on a missing tracker and assert the canonical CLI CommandError fallback. The final Node 22 instrumented run passes 1/1 and records DA:2088=2 and BRDA:2088,26,0,1. Both preflight outcomes are now explicit rather than incidental. The complete linked item-access tests pass 4/4. Earlier history was left append-only; this comment corrects the interpretation."
